# Video scripts for Module 1 (Essential and Emergency Newborn Care).
# Every narration line is taken from the manual (or, where marked FG, the
# facilitator guide); "film" says what the camera shows. Nothing here goes
# into a lesson: voiceover.py writes it to a Word file for recording.
S = {}
S['SN1.1.1'] = dict(
    title='Calling the neonatal team with SBAR', length='2 minutes',
    film=['Labour room: a midwife at the bedside of a mother in labour, CTG running.',
          'The midwife picks up the phone and calls the neonatal team. Split screen: the doctor answering.',
          'Each SBAR letter appears on screen as it is spoken.'],
    narration=[
        'Labour ward staff have primary responsibility for assessing the degree of risk anticipated and communicating their concerns effectively to the neonatal team. The earlier the neonatal team is given notice of a potential problem the better.',
        'If in doubt, call and discuss.',
        'When calling for neonatal assistance, the SBAR format should be used.',
        'S, Situation: "I’ve got a baby about to deliver with meconium and a non reassuring CTG."',
        'B, Background: "The baby is at term, mum has gestational diabetes, and there have been no other concerns in pregnancy. The obstetric registrar is setting up for a vacuum extraction in the room."',
        'A, Assessment: "The CTG trace is concerning, with late decelerations."',
        'R, Recommendation: "I need you to come to room 4 straight away. Will you need the registrar too?"',
        'Response: "I’ll come straight down, my registrar is with me. I’ll bring them along."',
        'The neonatal team should make every effort to attend promptly and ensure that they have adequate information to make management decisions.'])
S['SN1.1.2'] = dict(
    title='Preparing the resuscitation area and the quick equipment check', length='3 minutes',
    film=['A resuscitation area before a birth: radiant warmer, towels, hat, bag and masks, suction, oxygen, pulse oximeter.',
          'A health worker goes through the NRP quick equipment check, touching each item as it is named.',
          'Close-ups: flowmeter at 10 L/min; blender at 21%; term and preterm masks; laryngoscope blades 0 and 1.'],
    narration=[
        'NRP recommends prior preparation of standardized equipment kits to save time in an emergency.',
        'The prior resuscitation equipment check should be done with each call, even if the routine checkup has been done. It must be done quickly and in a systematic way.',
        'Warm: preheated warmer, warm towels or blankets, a hat, and a plastic bag or wrap for babies under 32 weeks.',
        'Clear airway: bulb syringe, and a 10F or 12F suction catheter attached to wall suction set at 80 to 100 mm Hg.',
        'Auscultate: stethoscope.',
        'Ventilate: flowmeter set to 10 litres per minute, a positive-pressure ventilation device, oxygen blender set to 21%, or 21 to 30% if under 35 weeks, term- and preterm-sized masks.',
        'Oxygenate: pulse oximeter with sensor and cover, and the newborn oxygen saturation table.',
        'Intubate: laryngoscope with size-0 and size-1 straight blades, endotracheal tubes 2.5, 3.0 and 3.5.',
        'Medicate: access to epinephrine and normal saline, and a table of pre-calculated emergency medication doses.',
        'Assign team roles clearly, ensure a warm environment, and confirm readiness verbally to the team.'])
S['SN1.1.3'] = dict(
    title='Early essential newborn care: the first minutes', length='2 minutes',
    film=['A vigorous term baby is born and placed on the mother\'s abdomen.',
          'Drying the baby thoroughly; gentle rubbing of the back; removing the wet cloth; skin-to-skin, covered, with a hat.',
          'The health worker watches breathing, tone, colour and activity.'],
    narration=[
        'All three rapid evaluation questions are yes: term, good tone, breathing or crying. When vigorous, the newborn stays with the mother, skin-to-skin.',
        'Provide warmth: maintain skin-to-skin contact on the mother’s chest or abdomen, and cover with a warm towel or blanket.',
        'Dry and stimulate: dry thoroughly to reduce heat loss, with gentle rubbing of the back or extremities to encourage effective breathing.',
        'Open the airway: position on the mother’s chest with a neutral head position.',
        'Clear secretions only if needed: wipe the mouth and nose with a cloth. Bulb suction only if secretions obstruct breathing.',
        'Ongoing monitoring: continue assessing breathing, tone, activity, colour and temperature.'])
S['SN1.1.4'] = dict(
    title='Four ways a newborn loses heat, and how to stop each', length='2 minutes',
    film=['Four short scenes, each with its name on screen: a baby on a cold scale; a fan and an open window; a wet baby just born; a cot next to a cold outside wall.',
          'After each scene, the correction: a warm blanket on the scale; fan off and window closed; immediate drying; cot moved away from the wall.'],
    narration=[
        'There are four ways in which a newborn loses body heat.',
        'Conduction: when the newborn is placed naked on a cooler surface, such as a table, a scale, a cold bed.',
        'Convection: when the newborn is exposed to cool surrounding air or to a draft from open doors, windows or fans.',
        'Evaporation: when amniotic fluid evaporates from the skin. This is the greatest source of heat loss at birth.',
        'Radiation: when the newborn is near cool objects, walls, tables and cabinets, without actually being in contact with them. This is the greatest source of heat loss after birth.',
        'Hypothermia is a temperature below 36.5 °C. Keep the core temperature between 36.5 and 37.5 °C at all times.'])
S['SN1.1.5'] = dict(
    title='Skin-to-skin contact and the ten steps of the warm chain', length='3 minutes',
    film=['Delivery room thermometer reading 25 °C or more; no fan.',
          'Immediate drying; baby placed naked on the mother\'s bare abdomen; both covered; hat on.',
          'Later scenes: first breastfeed; weighing on a warm blanket after the feed; dressed and wrapped; rooming-in.'],
    narration=[
        'The World Health Organization strongly recommends uninterrupted skin-to-skin contact for all mothers and newborns immediately after birth, for at least 90 minutes, or ideally longer.',
        'Warm delivery room: 25 °C or more, free from drafts. Adults should not determine temperature based on their comfort.',
        'Immediate drying with a warm towel to prevent heat loss by evaporation.',
        'Skin-to-skin contact: place the newborn on the mother’s chest or abdomen; cover with a second towel and put a cap on the head. Keep skin-to-skin during the delivery of the placenta, transfer and assessments.',
        'Breastfeeding: initiate as soon as possible, preferably within one hour of birth.',
        'Postpone weighing and bathing: weigh after skin-to-skin and the first feed, on a warm blanket. Bathing soon after birth causes a temperature drop.',
        'Appropriate clothing and blanket. Mother and newborn together, 24 hours a day, in a warm room.',
        'Warm transportation, and warm assessment on a warm surface when the baby is not skin-to-skin.'])
S['SN1.1.6'] = dict(
    title='Early essential newborn care for a breathing baby: the whole sequence', length='4 minutes',
    film=['Follow the manual\'s checklist in real time, with a clock on screen from the time of birth.',
          'Show: room temperature checked and fans off; two hand washings; dry cloth on the abdomen; bag and mask checked; two pairs of gloves.',
          'Birth: time called out; drying starts within 5 seconds; wet cloth removed; skin-to-skin; cover and hat.',
          'Check for a second baby; oxytocin to the mother within 1 minute; outer gloves off; cord pulsations checked; clamp at 2 cm, forceps at 5 cm.',
          'Delivery of the placenta; counselling the mother on feeding cues.'],
    narration=[
        'Pre-birth preparations: check the room temperature and turn off the fans. Tell the mother what is going to be done. Wash your hands. Place a dry cloth on the mother’s abdomen. Prepare the newborn resuscitation area, and check that the bag and mask are functioning. Wash your hands again, and put on two pairs of clean gloves.',
        'Call out the time of birth. Start drying within 5 seconds of birth. Dry the baby thoroughly: the eyes, face, head, front, back, arms and legs.',
        'Suction only if the airway is blocked and the baby is completely not breathing. Remove the wet cloth.',
        'Put the baby in direct skin-to-skin contact with the mother’s abdomen. Cover the baby’s body with a dry cloth and the head with a hat.',
        'Check for a second baby, and give oxytocin to the mother within one minute of delivery.',
        'Remove the outer pair of gloves. Check the cord pulsations, and clamp after the pulsations have stopped, usually one to three minutes. Place the clamp at 2 cm and the forceps at 5 cm from the umbilical base.',
        'Deliver the placenta, and counsel the mother on feeding cues: drooling, mouth opening, tonguing or licking, rooting, biting the hand, crawling.'])
S['SN1.2.1'] = dict(
    title='Recognising shock in a newborn', length='2 minutes',
    film=['A sick newborn on a warmer (manikin or consented baby).',
          'Pressing on the sternum for capillary refill with a timer; feeling hands and feet; feeling central and peripheral pulses; mottled skin close-up; heart rate on the monitor.'],
    narration=[
        'Shock, or circulatory failure, is a state of tissue hypoxia due to reduced oxygen delivery, increased oxygen consumption or inadequate oxygen utilization.',
        'Shock is often initially reversible, but must be recognized and treated immediately to prevent progression to irreversible organ dysfunction.',
        'Look for a fast or slow heart rate, cold extremities, poor capillary refill, mottling. Warm extremities may be seen in early warm shock.',
        'Hypotension is a late sign.',
        'Management priorities: immediate broad-spectrum antibiotics, fluid resuscitation, cardiovascular support for persistent hypotension, ventilation support, and close monitoring.',
        'Fluids: normal saline or Ringer’s lactate. Start with 20 ml per kg over 15 to 30 minutes. In cardiogenic shock, give a cautious bolus of 10 ml per kg and use inotropes.'])
S['SN1.2.2'] = dict(
    title='Checking blood glucose by heel prick', length='2 minutes',
    film=['Hand hygiene; warming the heel; the lateral heel puncture site; wiping away the first drop; the second drop onto the strip; reading the glucometer; recording on the bedside chart.'],
    narration=[
        'Plasma glucose from the laboratory is the most accurate. The point-of-care glucometer is used for screening; confirm low values with laboratory glucose if available.',
        'Heel-prick capillary sample: ensure a warm heel, wipe away the first drop, and collect the second drop.',
        'First screen at 1 to 2 hours of age, or before the first feed if the baby has signs. Repeat before feeds every 3 to 6 hours in at-risk infants until stable for 12 to 24 hours.',
        'In a baby with signs, check the glucose immediately.',
        'Hypoglycaemia is below 2 mmol/L in a term newborn, and below 2.6 mmol/L in a preterm newborn. Below 1 mmol/L is severe.',
        'Record each value on a simple bedside chart.'])
S['SN1.2.3'] = dict(
    title='Neonatal seizure or jitteriness?', length='3 minutes',
    film=['Real clinical clips (with consent) or high-quality teaching clips: focal clonic jerking; tonic posturing; subtle seizures (eye deviation, lip smacking).',
          'A jittery baby: rapid trembling that stops when the examiner gently holds the limb.',
          'On screen, the five features of the comparison table.'],
    narration=[
        'Is it a seizure, or a mimic such as jitteriness?',
        'Stimulus sensitivity: a seizure is not provoked by a stimulus. Jitteriness is often provoked or enhanced by handling.',
        'Movement pattern: a seizure is rhythmic and slow, fewer than four jerks a second, and localized. Jitteriness is tremor-like, rapid, oscillatory and generalized.',
        'Effect of restraint: a seizure persists; you can feel the muscle contracting. Jitteriness stops immediately with gentle restraint.',
        'Consciousness is often altered in a seizure; in jitteriness the infant is awake, or asleep but arousable.',
        'Eye signs: a seizure may have nystagmus or tonic deviation. In jitteriness the eyes are normal.',
        '(FG) Use STOP: Stimulus, Touch, Oscillation, Person. Treating a tremor is an error too.',
        'Then stabilise the airway, breathing and circulation, and look for the cause with SHOT: sugar and sepsis, hypoxia and history, osmolality and electrolytes, trauma, toxins and treatable metabolic causes.'])
S['SN1.3.1'] = dict(
    title='Vitamin K, eye care and cord care at 90 minutes', length='2 minutes',
    film=['A baby after the first breastfeed. Hand washing. Vitamin K drawn up; injection in the front, outer mid-thigh; needle into a sharps container.',
          'Eye medicine applied inside the lower lid of each eye.',
          'The cord: exposed, dry, nothing applied, not covered.'],
    narration=[
        'Give vitamin K to every newborn around 90 minutes of age. Because the injection is painful, it should not be given during the first hour after birth.',
        'The dose is 1 mg, or 0.5 mg for babies under 1500 grams, given intramuscularly in the front, outside of the mid-thigh. Wash your hands, and place used needles in a solid container with a lid.',
        'Eye care: applying medicine to the inside of the lower lid of both eyes soon after birth can prevent eye infections. It can be delayed until the baby has breastfed.',
        'Cord care: keep the cord exposed and dry. Do not apply anything to the cord unless a treatment is recommended by your health authority. Do not bandage or cover it. If soiled, wash with clean water. If there is blood from the cord, place a new tie tightly around it.'])
S['SN1.3.2'] = dict(
    title='Helping a mother with positioning and attachment', length='3 minutes',
    film=['A mother semi-reclined, baby held close; close-ups of the baby\'s body supported, head and body in line, nose opposite the nipple.',
          'Attachment close-up: wide open mouth, more areola above the lip, lower lip turned out, chin on the breast.',
          'Contrast: a poorly attached baby with only the nipple in the mouth.',
          'Signs of adequate feeding: swallowing, breast softening.'],
    narration=[
        'Support of breastfeeding after birth will improve the chances of success. Keep mother and baby together unless it is absolutely necessary to separate them.',
        'Help the mother to be comfortable, semi-reclined, with the baby held close, supported along the whole body, head and body in line, facing the breast, nose opposite the nipple.',
        'Signs of good attachment: more areola seen above the lips than below, mouth wide open, lower lip turned outward, chin touching the breast.',
        'Signs of poor attachment: only the nipple in the mouth, and pain.',
        'Signs that the baby is adequately fed: swallowing sounds, softening of the breast, feeding every 2 to 4 hours, 8 to 12 times a day, and sleeping well between feeds.'])
S['SN1.3.3'] = dict(
    title='Teaching a mother to hand express breast milk and cup feed', length='3 minutes',
    film=['A health worker teaches a mother to hand express into a clean cup.',
          'Cup feeding a small baby: baby upright, cup resting on the lower lip, baby laps the milk; never pour.'],
    narration=[
        'If breastfeeding has failed, the mother should be encouraged to express milk and give it by cup, spoon or syringe, and ensure feeds every 2 to 3 hours.',
        'To improve the flow of milk: apply warm compresses, massage the back and neck, and massage the breasts and nipples.',
        'For babies with a feeding difficulty: express breast milk, feed with a cup or tube, and move to exclusive breastfeeding.',
        '(FG) Show the cup technique slowly, and let the mother try while you watch.'],
    note='The manual gives the indications; the hand-expression and cup-feeding technique itself is demonstrated in the facilitator guide (Cup Feeding Technique). Qusay to confirm the technique steps to narrate.')
S['SN1.3.4'] = dict(
    title='Preparing and moving a newborn for referral', length='4 minutes',
    film=['A team of four around a sick preterm baby: team leader, nurse for airway and warmth, nurse for monitoring and documentation, one who makes the phone calls.',
          'Stabilising: temperature measured and corrected, airway position, pulses and CRT, nasogastric tube.',
          'Equipment check: oxygen cylinder, CPAP or T-piece, bag, transport incubator prewarmed, monitor.',
          'The phone handover to the NICU with read-back; documentation; the parents told; moving the baby; handover on arrival.'],
    narration=[
        'Transferring a newborn is a complex process that needs to be safe and well organized.',
        'Assess: vital signs, severity of distress, degree of maturity, and congenital anomalies or other complications. Decide the reason for admission, the level of care and the respiratory support needed.',
        'Stabilize: maintain normal body temperature, the airway and the circulation. Give antibiotics if indicated, and place a nasogastric tube for a distended abdomen.',
        'Check equipment: oxygen source, CPAP, T-piece, PPV bag or transport ventilator, transport incubator, monitors and infection control equipment. The team leader confirms the check was done.',
        'Organize the team and assign duties. A sick intubated preterm needs two or more medical and nursing staff.',
        'Document: gestational age, weight, diagnosis, serial vital signs and temperature before and after transfer, and any event during transport.',
        'Communicate: tell the parents the need and the reasons; phone the receiving NICU with the gestational age, diagnosis, level of care and respiratory support, and ask them to read it back.',
        'Transfer: use the safest available method, avoid delays, keep monitoring, and on arrival give a detailed handover.',
        '(FG) The commonest killer on the road is not the disease, it is the cold. Normalize the temperature before you start the transport.'])
